IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulations 10 to 14A: who is a credit institution, a financial institution, an auditor, an
-- insolvency practitioner, an external accountant, a tax adviser, an independent legal professional, a trust or
-- company service provider, an estate agent, a letting agent, a high value dealer, a casino, an auction
-- platform, an art market participant, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- HOW A DEFINITION READS HERE.  "X means a person who ..., when ..." answers JUST FALSE both for a person who is not in
-- the class the definition names and for a person in the class who is outside the "when" limit: a definition that says
-- "means" says no in its own words, and the "when" is part of the definition (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when in NOTES.md).
-- A term the Regulations borrow from another Act or instrument ("a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the
-- Companies Act 2006") is asked as a fact: a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Regulation 10 -- Credit institutions and financial institutions`

-- reg 10(1).  A credit institution is a credit institution as defined in the capital requirements regulation, or a UK
-- branch of one (or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country), when it accepts
-- deposits or other repayable funds from the public, grants credits for its own account, or bids directly in
-- auctions on behalf of its clients.
-- src:271 | (1) In these Regulations, “credit institution” means—
-- src:272 | (a) a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation; or
-- src:273 | (b) a branch (as defined by Article 4.1(17) of that regulation) located in the United Kingdom of an institution falling within sub-paragraph (a) (or an equivalent institution whose head office is located in a third country) wherever the institution's head office is located,
-- src:274 | when it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public or grants credits for its own account (within the meaning of the capital requirements regulation), or when it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients.
@ref reg 10(1) (src:271-274)
GIVEN `the person is a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a branch located in the United Kingdom of such an institution, or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it grants credits for its own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(1) the person is a credit institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation` OR `the person is a branch located in the United Kingdom of such an institution, or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“credit institution” means—"
        IF `it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` OR `it grants credits for its own account` OR `it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public or grants credits for its own account ..., or when it bids directly in auctions" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 10(4)(a).  "Listed activity" means an activity listed in points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 of Schedule 2.
-- FORK F4 (the keel's register, reading 2, chosen here): the rendering of Schedule 2 prints 13 items and no point numbers,
-- so the items carry the numbering of the Schedule's source list, with gaps: the first eleven printed items are points 2 to 12,
-- the twelfth ("Safe custody services") is point 14 and the thirteenth ("Issuing electronic money") is point 15.
-- That is the only reading under which reg 10(3)(c)'s "point 7" is a printed item (the sixth, trading for own account) and
-- reg 10(4)(a)'s "points 2 to 12, 14 and 15" is 13 points, the number of items printed.  The rendering alone cannot confirm it.
-- src:294 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation—
-- src:295 | (a) a “listed activity” means an activity listed in points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 of ... Schedule 2;
@ref reg 10(4)(a) (src:294-295)
GIVEN activity IS A `Listed activity`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 10(4)(a) the number of the point in Schedule 2 that lists the activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER activity
    WHEN `lending` THEN 2
    WHEN `financial leasing` THEN 3
    WHEN `payment services` THEN 4
    WHEN `issuing and administering other means of payment` THEN 5
    WHEN `guarantees and commitments` THEN 6
    WHEN `trading for own account or for account of customers` THEN 7
    WHEN `participation in securities issues and related services` THEN 8
    WHEN `advice to undertakings on capital structure, industrial strategy and mergers` THEN 9
    WHEN `money broking` THEN 10
    WHEN `portfolio management and advice` THEN 11
    WHEN `safekeeping and administration of securities` THEN 12
    WHEN `safe custody services` THEN 14
    WHEN `issuing electronic money` THEN 15

-- reg 10(4)(a), by the point's number: points 2 to 12, 14 and 15.  A point outside those numbers is not a listed
-- activity ("means").  The seat cannot ask this (the rendering prints no numbers); it is the paragraph's own words.
@ref reg 10(4)(a) (src:295-295)
GIVEN `the number of the point in Schedule 2` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(4)(a) the point of Schedule 2 is among points 2 to 12, 14 and 15` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the number of the point in Schedule 2` AT LEAST 2 AND `the number of the point in Schedule 2` AT MOST 12) OR `the number of the point in Schedule 2` EQUALS 14 OR `the number of the point in Schedule 2` EQUALS 15 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “listed activity” means an activity listed in points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 of ... Schedule 2"

-- reg 10(4)(a), the printed item asked directly: an activity of the Schedule's list is a listed activity when the point that
-- lists it is among points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 (fork F4, reading 2).
@ref reg 10(4)(a) (src:295-295)
GIVEN activity IS A `Listed activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(4)(a) the activity is a listed activity` MEANS
    `reg 10(4)(a) the point of Schedule 2 is among points 2 to 12, 14 and 15` (`reg 10(4)(a) the number of the point in Schedule 2 that lists the activity` activity)

-- reg 10(4)(b).  A pointer: "Regulated Activities Order" means the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated
-- Activities) Order 2001.
-- src:296 | (b) “Regulated Activities Order” means the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001.
@ref reg 10(4)(b) (src:296-296)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 10(4)(b) “Regulated Activities Order” means` MEANS
    "the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001"

-- reg 10(3)(a).  A credit institution is an institution referred to in paragraph (3): the answer of reg 10(1) is passed
-- through.
-- src:287 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a), the institutions referred to are—
-- src:288 | (a) a credit institution;
@ref reg 10(3)(a) (src:287-288)
GIVEN `reg 10(1) the person is a credit institution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(3)(a) the undertaking is a credit institution` MEANS `reg 10(1) the person is a credit institution`

-- reg 10(3)(b).  An undertaking whose only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement that falls within section
-- 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974, provides fixed sum credit in relation to the provision of services, and
-- provides financial accommodation by deferred payment or instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months.
-- src:289 | (b) an undertaking whose only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement which—
-- src:290 | (i) falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (debtor-creditor-supplier agreements);
-- src:291 | (ii) provides fixed sum credit (within the meaning given in section 10(1)(b) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (running-account credit and fixed-sum credit)) in relation to the provision of services; and
-- src:292 | (iii) provides financial accommodation by way of deferred payment or payment by instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months;
@ref reg 10(3)(b) (src:289-292)
GIVEN `its only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides fixed sum credit in relation to the provision of services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides financial accommodation by way of deferred payment or payment by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months over which the financial accommodation is provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(3)(b) the undertaking is one whose only listed activity is as a creditor under such an agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`its only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an undertaking whose only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement which"
        IF `the agreement falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974` AND `the agreement provides fixed sum credit in relation to the provision of services` AND `the agreement provides financial accommodation by way of deferred payment or payment by instalments` AND `the number of months over which the financial accommodation is provided` AT MOST 12 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) falls within section 12(a) ...; (ii) provides fixed sum credit ...; and (iii) provides financial accommodation ... over a period not exceeding 12 months" (a condition of the agreement is not met)

-- reg 10(3)(c).  An undertaking whose only listed activity is trading for its own account in one or more of the products in
-- point 7 of Schedule 2, where it does not have a customer ("customer" here is a person other than the undertaking that
-- is not a member of its group).  Point 7 is the printed item "Trading for own account or for account of customers"
-- (fork F4, reading 2).
-- src:293 | (c) an undertaking whose only listed activity is trading for its own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7 of ... Schedule 2 where the undertaking does not have a customer (and, for this purpose, “customer” means a person other than the undertaking which is not a member of the same group as the undertaking).
@ref reg 10(3)(c) (src:293-293)
GIVEN `the listed activities the undertaking carries out` IS A LIST OF `Listed activity`
      `its trading in the products listed in point 7 is for its own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a customer, that is a person other than the undertaking which is not a member of its group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(3)(c) the undertaking is one whose only listed activity is trading for its own account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the listed activities the undertaking carries out` EQUALS EMPTY) OR (NOT (all (GIVEN activity YIELD `reg 10(4)(a) the number of the point in Schedule 2 that lists the activity` activity EQUALS 7) `the listed activities the undertaking carries out` AND `its trading in the products listed in point 7 is for its own account`)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) an undertaking whose only listed activity is trading for its own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7"
        IF `it has a customer, that is a person other than the undertaking which is not a member of its group` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the undertaking does not have a customer"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- reg 10(3).  The institutions referred to are those of paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
-- src:287 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a), the institutions referred to are—
-- src:288 | (a) a credit institution;
-- src:289 | (b) an undertaking whose only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement which—
-- src:290 | (i) falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (debtor-creditor-supplier agreements);
-- src:291 | (ii) provides fixed sum credit (within the meaning given in section 10(1)(b) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (running-account credit and fixed-sum credit)) in relation to the provision of services; and
-- src:292 | (iii) provides financial accommodation by way of deferred payment or payment by instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months;
-- src:293 | (c) an undertaking whose only listed activity is trading for its own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7 of ... Schedule 2 where the undertaking does not have a customer (and, for this purpose, “customer” means a person other than the undertaking which is not a member of the same group as the undertaking).
@ref reg 10(3) (src:287-293)
GIVEN `the answers for paragraphs (3)(a), (3)(b) and (3)(c)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` MEANS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` `the answers for paragraphs (3)(a), (3)(b) and (3)(c)`

-- reg 10(2).  A financial institution is a person within one of paragraphs (a) to (i).  The Regulations' list is closed by
-- "means—".  Hand-gathered from the nine limbs (ruling E1, option B: guidance for gathering by hand), each of which also has
-- its own answer above (option C).
-- src:275 | (2) In these Regulations, “financial institution” means—
-- src:276 | (a) an undertaking, including a money service business, other than an institution referred to in paragraph (3), when the undertaking carries out one or more listed activity;
-- src:277 | (b) an authorised person (within the meaning of section 31 of FSMA), who has permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance, when carrying out or effecting any contract of long-term insurance other than a reinsurance contract (an “insurance undertaking”);
-- src:278 | (c) a person (other than a person falling within one of the exclusions to the definition of “investment firm” in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order), whose regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis, when—
-- src:279 | (i) providing investment services or performing investment activities (within the meaning of that article); or
-- src:280 | (ii) bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients;
-- src:281 | (d) a person falling within paragraph 1(k) of Part 1 of Schedule 3 to the Regulated Activities Order, when bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of clients of the person's main business;
-- src:282 | (e) a collective investment undertaking, when marketing or otherwise offering its units or shares;
-- src:283 | (f) an insurance intermediary as defined in article 33B(4) of the Regulated Activities Order, when it acts in respect of contracts of long-term insurance;
-- src:284 | (g) a branch located in the United Kingdom of a person referred to in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f) (or an equivalent person whose head office is located in a third country), wherever the person's head office is located, when carrying out any activity mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (f);
-- src:285 | (h) the National Savings Bank;
-- src:286 | (i) the Director of Savings, when money is raised under the auspices of the Director under the National Loans Act 1968 .
@ref reg 10(2) (src:275-286)
GIVEN `the answers for paragraphs (2)(a) to (2)(i)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(2) the person is a financial institution` MEANS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` `the answers for paragraphs (2)(a) to (2)(i)`

-- reg 10(2)(a).  An undertaking, including a money service business, other than an institution referred to in paragraph
-- (3), when it carries out one or more listed activity.
@ref reg 10(2)(a) (src:275-276)
GIVEN `the person is an undertaking, including a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2` IS A LIST OF `Listed activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(2)(a) the person is a financial institution as an undertaking carrying out a listed activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is an undertaking, including a money service business`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an undertaking, including a money service business"
        IF `reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an institution referred to in paragraph (3)"
        IF all (GIVEN activity YIELD `reg 10(4)(a) the activity is a listed activity` activity EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the undertaking carries out one or more listed activity" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition; the answer does not wait on paragraph (3), because an undertaking that carries out no listed activity is outside (a) whatever paragraph (3) says)
        IF `reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND any (GIVEN activity YIELD `reg 10(4)(a) the activity is a listed activity` activity EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3), or whether an activity it carries out is a listed activity, is not answered

-- SEAM S-10 (answering): regulation 55 (module mlr3) takes the answer to whether the person falls within regulation 10(2)(a).
@ref reg 10(2)(a) (src:275-276)
GIVEN `the person is an undertaking, including a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2` IS A LIST OF `Listed activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(2)(a) the person falls within regulation 10(2)(a)` MEANS
    `reg 10(2)(a) the person is a financial institution as an undertaking carrying out a listed activity` `the person is an undertaking, including a money service business` `reg 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` `the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2`

-- reg 10(2)(b).  An authorised person (section 31 FSMA) with permission under Part 4A FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of
-- insurance, when carrying out or effecting any contract of long-term insurance other than a reinsurance contract.
