GIVEN `the person is an authorised person with permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out or effecting a contract of long-term insurance that is not a reinsurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(2)(b) the person is a financial institution as an insurance undertaking` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is an authorised person with permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an authorised person (within the meaning of section 31 of FSMA), who has permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance"
        IF `it is carrying out or effecting a contract of long-term insurance that is not a reinsurance contract` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out or effecting any contract of long-term insurance other than a reinsurance contract" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

