      `it is providing investment services or performing investment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 10(2)(c) the person is a financial institution as an investment firm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`its regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) a person ... whose regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis"
        IF `the person falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of investment firm in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than a person falling within one of the exclusions to the definition of “investment firm” in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order)"
        IF `it is providing investment services or performing investment activities` OR `it is bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when— (i) providing investment services or performing investment activities ...; or (ii) bidding directly in auctions" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

