§ `Regulation 11 -- Auditors and others`

-- reg 11(a).  An auditor is a firm or individual who is (i) a statutory auditor (Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006), when carrying out
-- statutory audit work within section 1210 of that Act, or (ii) a local auditor (section 4(1) of the Local Audit and
-- Accountability Act 2014), when carrying out an audit required by that Act.
-- src:298 | In these Regulations—
-- src:299 | (a) “auditor” means any firm or individual who is—
-- src:300 | (i) a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006 (statutory auditors), when carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act (meaning of statutory auditor), or
-- src:301 | (ii) a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014 (general requirements for audit) , when carrying out an audit required by that Act.
@ref reg 11(a) (src:298-301)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out an audit required by that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 11(a) the person is an auditor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or individual` AND (`the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006` OR `the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014`)) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“auditor” means any firm or individual who is—"
        IF (`the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006` AND `it is carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act`) OR (`the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` AND `it is carrying out an audit required by that Act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out statutory audit work ..." and "when carrying out an audit required by that Act" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 11(b).  An insolvency practitioner is a firm or individual who acts as an insolvency practitioner within section 388 of the
-- Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989.
-- src:302 | (b) “insolvency practitioner” means any firm or individual who acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (meaning of “act as insolvency practitioner”).
@ref reg 11(b) (src:302-302)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 11(b) the person is an insolvency practitioner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a firm or individual` AND `it acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insolvency practitioner” means any firm or individual who acts as an insolvency practitioner"

-- reg 11(c).  An external accountant is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides accountancy services to other
-- persons, when providing such services.
-- src:303 | (c) “external accountant” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons, when providing such services.
@ref reg 11(c) (src:303-303)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 11(c) the person is an external accountant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“external accountant” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons"
        IF `it is providing such services` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when providing such services" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 11(d).  A tax adviser is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice,
-- in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, directly or through a third party, when providing such services.
-- src:304 | (d) “tax adviser” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party, when providing such services.
@ref reg 11(d) (src:304-304)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 11(d) the person is a tax adviser` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“tax adviser” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons"
        IF `it is providing such services` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when providing such services" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

§ `Regulation 12 -- Independent legal professionals and trust or company service providers`

-- reg 12(1)(a) to (e).  What a transaction concerns, for an independent legal professional.  Paragraph (e) is the last of five;
-- the list is the one the definition gives ("concerning—").
DECLARE `reg 12(1) what the transaction concerns` IS ONE OF
    `reg 12(1)(a) the buying and selling of real property or business entities`
    `reg 12(1)(b) the managing of client money, securities or other assets`
    `reg 12(1)(c) the opening or management of bank, savings or securities accounts`
    `reg 12(1)(d) the organisation of contributions necessary for the creation, operation or management of companies`
    `reg 12(1)(e) the creation, operation or management of trusts, companies, foundations or similar structures`
    `reg 12(1) something else`

-- reg 12(1).  An independent legal professional is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial
-- services to others, when participating in financial or real property transactions concerning (a) to (e); a person participates
-- by assisting in the planning or execution of the transaction or otherwise acting for or on behalf of a client in it.
-- src:306 | (1) In these Regulations, “independent legal professional” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons, when participating in financial or real property transactions concerning—
-- src:307 | (a) the buying and selling of real property or business entities;
-- src:308 | (b) the managing of client money, securities or other assets;
-- src:309 | (c) the opening or management of bank, savings or securities accounts;
-- src:310 | (d) the organisation of contributions necessary for the creation, operation or management of companies; or
-- src:311 | (e) the creation, operation or management of trusts, companies, foundations or similar structures,
-- src:312 | and, for this purpose, a person participates in a transaction by assisting in the planning or execution of the transaction or otherwise acting for or on behalf of a client in the transaction.
@ref reg 12(1) (src:306-312)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assists in the planning or execution of the transaction, or otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the financial or real property transaction concerns` IS A `reg 12(1) what the transaction concerns`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 12(1) the person is an independent legal professional` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“independent legal professional” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons"
        IF `it assists in the planning or execution of the transaction, or otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction` AND (NOT (`what the financial or real property transaction concerns` EQUALS `reg 12(1) something else`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when participating in financial or real property transactions concerning— (a) ... (e)" and "a person participates in a transaction by assisting in the planning or execution of the transaction or otherwise acting for or on behalf of a client" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 12(2).  The services of a trust or company service provider.
DECLARE `reg 12(2) service` IS ONE OF
    `reg 12(2)(a) forming a firm`
    `reg 12(2)(ab) selling an off-the-shelf firm`
    `reg 12(2)(b)(i) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a director or secretary of a company`
    `reg 12(2)(b)(ii) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a partner of a partnership`
    `reg 12(2)(b)(iii) acting, or arranging for another person to act, in a similar capacity in relation to other legal persons`
    `reg 12(2)(c) providing a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address or other related services for a company, partnership or any other legal person or legal arrangement`
    `reg 12(2)(d)(i) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a trustee of an express trust or similar legal arrangement`
    `reg 12(2)(d)(ii) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder`
    `reg 12(2) another service`

-- reg 12(2).  A trust or company service provider is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides any of the services
-- listed, when providing such services.  A nominee shareholder counts only for "a person other than a company whose securities
-- are listed on a regulated market".
-- src:313 | (2) In these Regulations, “trust or company service provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides any of the following services to other persons, when that firm or practitioner is providing such services—
-- src:314 | (a) forming a firm;
-- src:315 | (ab) selling an off-the-shelf firm;
-- src:316 | (b) acting, or arranging for another person to act—
-- src:317 | (i) as a director or secretary of a company;
-- src:318 | (ii) as a partner of a partnership; or
-- src:319 | (iii) in a similar capacity in relation to other legal persons;
-- src:320 | (c) providing a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address or other related services for a company, partnership or any other legal person or legal arrangement;
-- src:321 | (d) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as—
-- src:322 | (i) a trustee of an express trust or similar legal arrangement; or
-- src:323 | (ii) a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market.
@ref reg 12(2) (src:313-323)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business provides these services to other persons` IS A LIST OF `reg 12(2) service`
      `where it acts as a nominee shareholder, the person it acts for is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 12(2) the person is a trust or company service provider` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND any (GIVEN service YIELD (NOT (service EQUALS `reg 12(2) another service`)) AND (NOT (service EQUALS `reg 12(2)(d)(ii) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder` AND `where it acts as a nominee shareholder, the person it acts for is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market`))) `it by way of business provides these services to other persons`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trust or company service provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides any of the following services to other persons" and "(ii) a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market"
        IF `it is providing such services` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when that firm or practitioner is providing such services" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 12(3).  An off-the-shelf firm is a firm that either does not carry on business, or carries on business that is not the main
-- activity carried on by the trust or company service provider.
-- src:324 | (3) In this regulation, an “off-the-shelf firm” means a firm that either—
-- src:325 | (a) does not carry on business; or
-- src:326 | (b) carries on business but such business is not the main activity carried on by the trust or company service provider.
@ref reg 12(3) (src:324-326)
GIVEN `the firm carries on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that business is the main activity carried on by the trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 12(3) the firm is an off-the-shelf firm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the firm carries on business`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (`that business is the main activity carried on by the trust or company service provider`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “off-the-shelf firm” means a firm that either— (a) does not carry on business; or (b) carries on business but such business is not the main activity"

§ `Regulation 13 -- Estate agents and letting agents`

-- reg 13(2).  Estate agency work is read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979, but references there to
-- disposing of or acquiring an interest in land are (despite section 2) taken to include an estate or interest in land outside the
-- United Kingdom that is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest.
DECLARE `reg 13(2) dealing in land` HAS
    `the estate or interest is in land in the United Kingdom`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the estate or interest is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:329 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1) “estate agency work” is to be read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979 (estate agency work), but for those purposes references in that section to disposing of or acquiring an interest in land are (despite anything in section 2 of that Act) to be taken to include references to disposing of or acquiring an estate or interest in land outside the United Kingdom where that estate or interest is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest.
@ref reg 13(2) (src:329-329)
GIVEN dealing IS A `reg 13(2) dealing in land`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2) the dealing counts as disposing of or acquiring an interest in land for estate agency work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF dealing's `the estate or interest is in land in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF dealing's `the estate or interest is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the paragraph adds an estate or interest in land outside the United Kingdom "where that estate or interest is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest"; section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979 decides what else is estate agency work

-- reg 13(1).  An estate agent is a firm or sole practitioner who, or whose employees, carry out estate agency work, when the work is
-- being carried out.
-- src:328 | (1) In these Regulations, “estate agent” means a firm or a sole practitioner, who, or whose employees, carry out estate agency work, when the work is being carried out.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:328-328)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it, or its employees, carry out estate agency work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is being carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(1) the person is an estate agent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it, or its employees, carry out estate agency work`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“estate agent” means a firm or a sole practitioner, who, or whose employees, carry out estate agency work"
        IF `the work is being carried out` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the work is being carried out" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 13(4)(b)(ii).  The monthly rent at which letting agency work begins: £10,000.
-- src:337 | (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
@ref reg 13(4)(b)(ii) (src:337-337)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 13(4)(b)(ii) the monthly rent of 10000 pounds sterling` MEANS 10000

-- reg 13(4).  Letting agency work is work (a) done in response to instructions from a prospective landlord seeking to find a person
-- to let to, or a prospective tenant seeking to find land to rent, and (b) done in a case where an agreement is concluded for
-- the letting of land for a term of a month or more at a rent that during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a
-- monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
-- src:331 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (3), “letting agency work” means work—
-- src:332 | (a) consisting of things done in response to instructions received from—
-- src:333 | (i) a person (a “prospective landlord”) seeking to find another person to whom to let land, or
-- src:334 | (ii) a person (a “prospective tenant”) seeking to find land to rent, and
-- src:335 | (b) done in a case where an agreement is concluded for the letting of land—
-- src:336 | (i) for a term of a month or more, and
-- src:337 | (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
@ref reg 13(4) (src:331-337)
GIVEN `the work is done in response to instructions received from a prospective landlord seeking to find another person to whom to let land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is done in response to instructions received from a prospective tenant seeking to find land to rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement is concluded for the letting of land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of the letting, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(4) the work is letting agency work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the work is done in response to instructions received from a prospective landlord seeking to find another person to whom to let land` OR `the work is done in response to instructions received from a prospective tenant seeking to find land to rent`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“letting agency work” means work— (a) consisting of things done in response to instructions received from— (i) a person (a “prospective landlord”) seeking to find another person to whom to let land, or (ii) a person (a “prospective tenant”) seeking to find land to rent"
        IF NOT (`an agreement is concluded for the letting of land`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) done in a case where an agreement is concluded for the letting of land"
        IF `the term of the letting, in months` AT LEAST 1 AND `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 13(4)(b)(ii) the monthly rent of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) for a term of a month or more, and (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more"

-- reg 13(6).  The things that are not letting agency work when done alone.
DECLARE `reg 13(6) thing done` IS ONE OF
    `reg 13(6)(a) publishing advertisements or disseminating information`
    `reg 13(6)(b) providing a means by which a prospective landlord or a prospective tenant can, in response to an advertisement or dissemination of information, make direct contact with a prospective tenant or a prospective landlord`
    `reg 13(6)(c) providing a means by which a prospective landlord and a prospective tenant can communicate directly with each other`
    `reg 13(6)(d) the provision of legal or notarial services by a barrister, advocate, solicitor or other legal representative communications with whom may be the subject of a claim to professional privilege or, in Scotland, protected from disclosure in legal proceedings on grounds of confidentiality of communication`
    `reg 13(6) another thing`

-- reg 13(5) and (6).  The things listed in paragraph (6) are not letting agency work when done by a firm or sole practitioner (or their
-- employees) if neither they nor any of their employees does anything else within paragraph (4).
-- src:338 | (5) For the purposes of paragraph (3) “letting agency work” does not include the things listed in paragraph (6) when done by, or by employees of, a firm or sole practitioner if neither the firm or sole practitioner, nor any of their employees, does anything else within paragraph (4).
-- src:339 | (6) Those things are—
-- src:340 | (a) publishing advertisements or disseminating information;
-- src:341 | (b) providing a means by which a prospective landlord or a prospective tenant can, in response to an advertisement or dissemination of information, make direct contact with a prospective tenant or a prospective landlord;
-- src:342 | (c) providing a means by which a prospective landlord and a prospective tenant can communicate directly with each other;
-- src:343 | (d) the provision of legal or notarial services by a barrister, advocate, solicitor or other legal representative communications with whom may be the subject of a claim to professional privilege or, in Scotland, protected from disclosure in legal proceedings on grounds of confidentiality of communication.
@ref reg 13(5) and (6) (src:338-343)
GIVEN thing IS A `reg 13(6) thing done`
      `the firm or sole practitioner, or any of their employees, does anything else within paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(5) the thing done is letting agency work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF thing EQUALS `reg 13(6) another thing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (5) speaks only of "the things listed in paragraph (6)" (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)
        IF `the firm or sole practitioner, or any of their employees, does anything else within paragraph (4)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if neither the firm or sole practitioner, nor any of their employees, does anything else within paragraph (4)" (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“letting agency work” does not include the things listed in paragraph (6)"

-- reg 13(3).  A letting agent is a firm or sole practitioner who, or whose employees, carry out letting agency work, when carrying out
-- such work.
-- src:330 | (3) In these Regulations, “letting agent” means a firm or sole practitioner who, or whose employees, carry out letting agency work, when carrying out such work.
@ref reg 13(3) (src:330-330)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it, or its employees, carry out letting agency work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out such work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(3) the person is a letting agent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it, or its employees, carry out letting agency work`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“letting agent” means a firm or sole practitioner who, or whose employees, carry out letting agency work"
        IF `it is carrying out such work` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out such work" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 13(7).  In paragraph (4), "land" includes part of a building and part of any other structure.
DECLARE `reg 13(7) what is let` IS ONE OF
    `reg 13(7) land`
    `reg 13(7) part of a building`
    `reg 13(7) part of any other structure`
    `reg 13(7) something else`

-- src:344 | (7) In paragraph (4) “land” includes part of a building and part of any other structure.
@ref reg 13(7) (src:344-344)
GIVEN `what is let` IS A `reg 13(7) what is let`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(7) the thing let is land for paragraph (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what is let`
    WHEN `reg 13(7) land` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 13(7) part of a building` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 13(7) part of any other structure` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 13(7) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“land” includes part of a building and part of any other structure"

§ `Regulation 14 -- High value dealers, casinos, auction platforms and art market participants`

-- reg 14(1)(a).  The cash figure for a high value dealer: £10,000 in total.
-- src:346 | (1) In these Regulations—
-- src:347 | (a) “high value dealer” means a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods (including an auctioneer dealing in goods), when the trader makes or receives, in respect of any transaction, a payment or payments in cash of at least £10,000 in total, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked;
@ref reg 14(1)(a) (src:346-347)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 14(1)(a) the cash payments of 10000 pounds sterling in total` MEANS 10000

-- reg 14(1)(a).  A high value dealer is a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods (including an auctioneer dealing in
-- goods), when it makes or receives, in respect of any transaction, a payment or payments in cash of at least £10,000 in total,
-- whether in a single operation or in several operations that appear to be linked.
@ref reg 14(1)(a) (src:347-347)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole trader` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business trades in goods, including as an auctioneer dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total of the payments in cash it makes or receives in respect of the transaction, in single or linked operations, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(a) the person is a high value dealer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole trader` AND `it by way of business trades in goods, including as an auctioneer dealing in goods`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“high value dealer” means a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods (including an auctioneer dealing in goods)"
        IF `the total of the payments in cash it makes or receives in respect of the transaction, in single or linked operations, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 14(1)(a) the cash payments of 10000 pounds sterling in total` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the trader makes or receives, in respect of any transaction, a payment or payments in cash of at least £10,000 in total" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 14(1)(b).  A casino is the holder of a casino operating licence (section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005).
-- src:348 | (b) “casino” means the holder of a casino operating licence and, for this purpose, a “casino operating licence” has the meaning given by section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005 (nature of licence);
@ref reg 14(1)(b) (src:348-348)
GIVEN `the person holds a casino operating licence, that is a licence within section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(b) the person is a casino` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person holds a casino operating licence, that is a licence within section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“casino” means the holder of a casino operating licence"

-- reg 14(1)(c).  An auction platform is a platform which auctions two-day spot or five-day futures (within regulation 2(1) of the UK
-- auctioning regulations), when it carries out activities covered by that regulation.
-- src:349 | (c) “auction platform” means a platform which auctions two-day spot or five-day futures, within the meanings given by regulation 2(1) of the UK auctioning regulations, when it carries out activities covered by that regulation.
@ref reg 14(1)(c) (src:349-349)
GIVEN `the person is a platform which auctions two-day spot or five-day futures, within the meanings given by regulation 2(1) of the UK auctioning regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it carries out activities covered by that regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(c) the person is an auction platform` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a platform which auctions two-day spot or five-day futures, within the meanings given by regulation 2(1) of the UK auctioning regulations`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“auction platform” means a platform which auctions two-day spot or five-day futures"
        IF `it carries out activities covered by that regulation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when it carries out activities covered by that regulation" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 14(3).  A firm or sole practitioner is not an art market participant for paragraph (1)(d)(i) in relation to the sale of a work of
-- art created by, or attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner.
-- src:358 | (3) A firm or sole practitioner is not an art market participant for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)(i) in relation to the sale of a work of art which is created by, or is attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner.
@ref reg 14(3) (src:358-358)
GIVEN `the sale is of a work of art created by, or attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sale is of a work of art created by, or attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not an art market participant for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)(i) in relation to the sale of a work of art which is created by, or is attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of the sale of a work of art created by, or attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner

-- reg 14(1)(d)(i) and (ii).  The figure for an art market participant: £10,000 or more.
-- src:350 | (d) “art market participant” means , subject to paragraph (3), a firm or sole practitioner who—
-- src:351 | (i) by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art and the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, amounts to £10,000 or more; or
-- src:352 | (ii) is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, by way of business stores works of art in the freeport and the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more;
@ref reg 14(1)(d) (src:350-352)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 14(1)(d) the art transaction or storage value of 10000 pounds sterling` MEANS 10000

-- reg 14(1)(d)(i).  A firm or sole practitioner who by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or
-- purchase of, works of art and the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, amounts to £10,000 or more.
-- Subject to paragraph (3): not an art market participant "for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)(i)" in relation to the sale of a
-- work of art created by, or attributable to, a member of the firm or the sole practitioner.
@ref reg 14(1)(d)(i) (src:350-351)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the transaction, or of a series of linked transactions, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
      `reg 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(d)(i) the person is an art market participant as a trader or intermediary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art` AND `the value of the transaction, or of a series of linked transactions, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 14(1)(d) the art transaction or storage value of 10000 pounds sterling`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“art market participant” means , subject to paragraph (3), a firm or sole practitioner who— (i) by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art and the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, amounts to £10,000 or more"
        IF `reg 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to paragraph (3)" and "is not an art market participant for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)(i)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- reg 14(1)(d)(ii).  A firm or sole practitioner who is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner,
-- by way of business stores works of art in the freeport and the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of
-- linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more.
@ref reg 14(1)(d)(ii) (src:352-352)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, by way of business stores works of art in the freeport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(d)(ii) the person is an art market participant as the operator of a freeport` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND `it is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, by way of business stores works of art in the freeport` AND `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, in pounds sterling` AT LEAST `reg 14(1)(d) the art transaction or storage value of 10000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, by way of business stores works of art in the freeport and the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more"

-- reg 14(1)(d).  An art market participant is a person within (i) or (ii); "means" closes the list.  Hand-gathered from the two limbs
-- (ruling E1, option B: guidance for gathering by hand); each limb also has its own answer above (option C).
@ref reg 14(1)(d) (src:350-352)
GIVEN `the answers for sub-paragraphs (d)(i) and (d)(ii)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(d) the person is an art market participant` MEANS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` `the answers for sub-paragraphs (d)(i) and (d)(ii)`

-- reg 14(1)(e).  A freeport is a warehouse or storage facility within an area the Treasury designated as a special area for customs
-- purposes under section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979.
-- src:353 | (e) “freeport” means a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (designation of free zones) ;
@ref reg 14(1)(e) (src:353-353)
GIVEN `the place is a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(e) the place is a freeport` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place is a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“freeport” means a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury"

-- reg 14(1)(f).  A work of art is anything that, under section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, is a work of art for section
-- 21(5)(a) of that Act.
-- src:354 | (f) “work of art” means anything which, in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994 (value of imported goods) , is a work of art for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act.
@ref reg 14(1)(f) (src:354-354)
GIVEN `the thing is, in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, a work of art for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(1)(f) the thing is a work of art` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is, in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, a work of art for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work of art” means anything which, in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, is a work of art"

-- reg 14(2).  A payment does not cease to be a "payment in cash" for paragraph (1)(a) if cash is paid by or on behalf of the person making
-- it (a) to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party, or (b) into a bank account for the benefit of the other
-- party.
-- src:355 | (2) A payment does not cease to be a “payment in cash” for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a) if cash is paid by or on behalf of the person making the payment—
-- src:356 | (a) to a person other than the other party to the transaction for the benefit of the other party, or
-- src:357 | (b) into a bank account for the benefit of the other party to the transaction.
@ref reg 14(2) (src:355-357)
GIVEN `the payment is made in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cash is paid, by or on behalf of the person making the payment, to a person other than the other party to the transaction for the benefit of the other party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cash is paid, by or on behalf of the person making the payment, into a bank account for the benefit of the other party to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14(2) the payment is a payment in cash for paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is made in cash` AND (`the cash is paid, by or on behalf of the person making the payment, to a person other than the other party to the transaction for the benefit of the other party` OR `the cash is paid, by or on behalf of the person making the payment, into a bank account for the benefit of the other party to the transaction`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says only that a payment in cash "does not cease to be" one in the two cases; what else is cash is for the definition of "cash" in regulation 3(1)

§ `Regulation 14A -- Cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers`

-- reg 14A(3)(a).  A cryptoasset is a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights that uses a form of
-- distributed ledger technology and can be transferred, stored or traded electronically.
-- SEAM S-13 (answering): reg 64B takes this answer as the input `reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset`.
-- src:368 | (3) For the purposes of this regulation—
-- src:369 | (a) “cryptoasset” means a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights that uses a form of distributed ledger technology and can be transferred, stored or traded electronically;
@ref reg 14A(3)(a) (src:368-369)
GIVEN `it is cryptographically secured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a digital representation of value or contractual rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it uses a form of distributed ledger technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be transferred, stored or traded electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is cryptographically secured` AND `it is a digital representation of value or contractual rights` AND `it uses a form of distributed ledger technology` AND `it can be transferred, stored or traded electronically` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset” means a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights that uses a form of distributed ledger technology and can be transferred, stored or traded electronically"

-- reg 14A(3)(c).  In paragraph (1)(a), (b) and (c), "cryptoasset" includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset.
-- src:375 | (c) in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of paragraph (1), “cryptoasset” includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset.
@ref reg 14A(3)(c) (src:375-375)
GIVEN `reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a right to, or interest in, a cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14A(3)(c) the thing is a cryptoasset for sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 14A(3)(a) the thing is a cryptoasset` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the thing is a right to, or interest in, a cryptoasset` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“cryptoasset” includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset"

-- reg 14A(3)(b).  What "money" is for this regulation: sterling, any other currency, or any other medium of exchange, but not a cryptoasset.
DECLARE `reg 14A(3)(b) kind of thing exchanged` IS ONE OF
    `reg 14A(3)(b)(i) money in sterling`
    `reg 14A(3)(b)(ii) money in any other currency`
    `reg 14A(3)(b)(iii) money in any other medium of exchange`
    `reg 14A(3)(b) a cryptoasset`
    `reg 14A(3)(b) something else`

-- src:370 | (b) “money” means—
-- src:371 | (i) money in sterling,
-- src:372 | (ii) money in any other currency, or
-- src:373 | (iii) money in any other medium of exchange,
-- src:374 | but does not include a cryptoasset; and
@ref reg 14A(3)(b) (src:370-374)
GIVEN thing IS A `reg 14A(3)(b) kind of thing exchanged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14A(3)(b) the thing is money` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `reg 14A(3)(b)(i) money in sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 14A(3)(b)(ii) money in any other currency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 14A(3)(b)(iii) money in any other medium of exchange` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 14A(3)(b) a cryptoasset` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include a cryptoasset"
    WHEN `reg 14A(3)(b) something else` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“money” means— (i) money in sterling, (ii) money in any other currency, or (iii) money in any other medium of exchange"

-- reg 14A(1).  The services of a cryptoasset exchange provider.
DECLARE `reg 14A(1) service` IS ONE OF
    `reg 14A(1)(a) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets`
    `reg 14A(1)(b) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, one cryptoasset for another`
    `reg 14A(1)(c) operating a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets`
    `reg 14A(1) another service`

-- reg 14A(1).  A cryptoasset exchange provider is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides one or more of the services
-- (a) to (c), including as creator or issuer of any of the cryptoassets involved, when providing such services.
-- src:360 | (1) In these Regulations, “cryptoasset exchange provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides one or more of the following services, including where the firm or sole practitioner does so as creator or issuer of any of the cryptoassets involved, when providing such services—
-- src:361 | (a) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets,
-- src:362 | (b) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, one cryptoasset for another, or
-- src:363 | (c) operating a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets.
@ref reg 14A(1) (src:360-363)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it by way of business provides these services` IS A LIST OF `reg 14A(1) service`
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14A(1) the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND any (GIVEN service YIELD NOT (service EQUALS `reg 14A(1) another service`)) `it by way of business provides these services`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset exchange provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides one or more of the following services"
        IF `it is providing such services` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when providing such services" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

-- reg 14A(2).  What a custodian wallet provider safeguards.
DECLARE `reg 14A(2) what is safeguarded` IS ONE OF
    `reg 14A(2)(a) cryptoassets on behalf of its customers`
    `reg 14A(2)(b) private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers in order to hold, store and transfer cryptoassets`
    `reg 14A(2) something else`

-- reg 14A(2).  A custodian wallet provider is a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard
-- and administer, (a) cryptoassets or (b) private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers, when providing such services.
-- src:364 | (2) In these Regulations, “custodian wallet provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer—
-- src:365 | (a) cryptoassets on behalf of its customers, or
-- src:366 | (b) private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers in order to hold, store and transfer cryptoassets,
-- src:367 | when providing such services.
@ref reg 14A(2) (src:364-367)
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what it by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer` IS A LIST OF `reg 14A(2) what is safeguarded`
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14A(2) the person is a custodian wallet provider` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a firm or sole practitioner` AND any (GIVEN safeguarded YIELD NOT (safeguarded EQUALS `reg 14A(2) something else`)) `what it by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“custodian wallet provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer"
        IF `it is providing such services` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when providing such services" (Assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" in a definition that says "means" is part of the definition)

